r_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.5987268288699943,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.19484303240338718,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.018525546179485944,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":31.7,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.013376330702751016,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":66.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009716666872208908,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":83.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.24765,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.167,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":16.7,"pf":[],"description_full":"Greenlight Capital Re, Ltd., through its subsidiaries, operates as a property and casualty reinsurance company worldwide. It operates through Open Market and Innovations segments. The company offers casualty reinsurance, such as automobile liability and general liability. It also provides coverages for casualty, including general liability, umbrella, multiline casualty, and workers' compensation; financial, such as mortgage, trade credit, surety, transactional liability, and financial multiline; health, which include primarily accident and critical illness; multiline comprising FAL business, coupled with multiline commercial and personal auto liability, BOP, and multiline commercial; property, including commercial property and property catastrophe; and specialty products and services, such as agriculture, cyber, marine and energy, aviation and space, specialty multiline, and WPVT which covers losses relating to war, political violence, and terrorism. The company markets its products through reinsurance brokers. Greenlight Capital Re, Ltd. was incorporated in 2004 and is headquartered in Grand Cayman, the Cayman Islands.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Greg  Richardson | CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 84 people. Revenue per employee of $8.7M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $2.5M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $84K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Greenlight Reinsurance, Ltd. is a small-cap financial services business with a $530M market cap on $730M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +19% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $210M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.81\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 16\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 25% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (83% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.167},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 88% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (GLRE)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/40/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_GLRE_111126020002_1794423602.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794423602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Analysis: Greenlight Capital Re (NASDAQ:GLRE) versus Brown & Brown (NYSE:BRO)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/financial-analysis-greenlight-capital-re-nasdaqglre-versus-brown-brown-nysebro.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794240904.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"